## OpenAPI as Source of Truth

The API contract lives in `api/v1alpha1/openapi.yaml`. Server stubs and types are generated by oapi-codegen. Never hand-edit generated files.

## Code Generation

- Server interface + types generated from OpenAPI spec
- Handlers implement the generated `ServerInterface`
- Request validation handled by `nethttp-middleware` (OpenAPI validator) — handlers do NOT re-validate fields the middleware already checks

## Adding/Changing API Endpoints

1. Edit `api/v1alpha1/openapi.yaml`
2. Run code generation (`make generate` or oapi-codegen command)
3. Implement the new method on the handler struct
4. DO NOT add redundant request validation that the OpenAPI middleware already enforces
